      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough was once home to Marconi Wireless Telegraph’s factory and lab, and in 1921 it launched WDY, New Jersey’s first licensed radio station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roselle_Park%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Roselle Park’s historic 1.3‑square‑mile area was originally part of Elizabethtown before becoming its own borough in the late 19th century.",
